{"title":"1976 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 18th <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a> 1976 in Austria.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In a convex quadrilateral (in the plane) with the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/f/6ffeefc5e83cc7e410235362f631f1283068f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32 \\text{ cm}^{2}$\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> the sum of two opposite sides and a diagonal is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e492161a5ed4df894fa26cff08483fea26779f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />. Determine all the possible values that the other diagonal can have.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b28e1313eb2184d873000fe53a4a1e275ad49922.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{1}(x) = x^{2} - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/5/1e5d2a6536838586e16969ed7624d38735b533ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{j}(x) = P_{1}(P_{j - 1}(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/0/c20f6924610fa28a80df6356a38b8ca9f2b7e1fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j= 2,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" /> Prove that for any positive integer n the roots of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/3/943ca2e4b290bc9dbe4189a5af139ceea1d8aeb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{n}(x) = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> are all real and distinct.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A box whose shape is a parallelepiped can be completely filled with cubes of side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdd1b53e5faf7a118222e4b7571d1e9afa0cf56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> If we put in it the maximum possible number of cubes, each of volume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, with the sides parallel to those of the box, then exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> percent from the volume of the box is occupied. Determine the possible dimensions of the box.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find the largest number obtainable as the product of positive integers whose sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/4/b146679dc9b3c5ecc337c4b90450a40e0283f6ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1976$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let a set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> equations be given, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/d/33d265f9898583a35809dd0724fa4a1ff07410ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{ccccccc} a_{11}x_1&amp;+&amp;\\cdots&amp;+&amp;a_{1q}x_q&amp;=&amp;0,\\\\ a_{21}x_1&amp;+&amp;\\cdots&amp;+&amp;a_{2q}x_q&amp;=&amp;0,\\\\ &amp;&amp;&amp;\\vdots&amp;&amp;&amp;\\\\ a_{p1}x_1&amp;+&amp;\\cdots&amp;+&amp;a_{pq}x_q&amp;=&amp;0,\\\\ \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"262\" height=\"90\" />\nwith coefficients <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/b/d6b159fdba4b71ff0eb9caee9a10fb34ebfcaad8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{ij}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e4a2a62f374328249794df8b2cdd1a2e9f949d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{ij}=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/7/1178af8fcc5f3f3acb9f151f7dcc2c4eefe88fd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cd84e4dac728fd6c7c74de56e237cf72c609ed0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1,\\dots, p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"89\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f7707e9778f6f50672f48e6073a70578db61c0b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j=1,\\dots, q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" />. Prove that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/6/db667bfd8232800e87282b42ff9c33c9c6b37c74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=2p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />, there exists a solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/6/a86b7d2c37fc55d53d0f5cafcd2abfd787dcb23c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, \\dots, x_q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" /> of this system such that all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/0/ac0e6fa105993ce976db0dc241d59ab8e68e6efc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f7707e9778f6f50672f48e6073a70578db61c0b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j=1,\\dots, q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" />) are integers satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/6/4065915033e555eb1b05af2d3e88bcce2e57e826.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x_j|\\le q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/5/ed51c3433e3372ab8f19643e03f2d3208d82fdc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_j\\ne 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> for at least one value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For all positive integral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/7/3575cb2fb553b355f4e4d07325736f4c1fff8e31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u_{n+1}=u_n(u_{n-1}^2-2)-u_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"200\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1b9b9d1edac531ae0fd6ec80c83d8405a054860.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u_0=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/1/fd132c38d1f904b420de91954748cca7aa2ecfc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u_1=2\\frac12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"62\" height=\"37\" />. Prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/c/b3ce5b1c837946b02ba07b5d554d866768556374.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3\\log_2[u_n]=2^n-(-1)^n,\\]\" width=\"187\" height=\"18\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/e/bceb7b14e55d33a8bca29b7863ad3cdae95afce4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[x]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" /> is the integral part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO\" title=\"1976 IMO\">1976 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=1&amp;cid=16&amp;year=1976\">IMO 1976 Problems on the Resources page</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO\" title=\"1976 IMO\">1976 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_IMO\" title=\"1975 IMO\">1975 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO\" title=\"1977 IMO\">1977 IMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018042358\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 197/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 837/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5917/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.449      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.449      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7776:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018042358 and revision id 143926. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}